// Rule: [T1218.011] Clearfake - WebDAV RUNDLL32 Ordinal
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1218.011
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: Defender XDR hunt for source-observed execution of disguised DLLs directly from WebDAV UNC paths through export ordinal #1.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceProcessEvents for webdav rundll32 ordinal using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A result proves that the published query conditions matched in DeviceProcessEvents; it is an investigative event, not a malicious verdict.
// A match does not prove: A match does not establish ClickFix delivery, Amatera execution, credential theft, NetSupport installation, C2, or compromise.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// ClearFake WebDAV rundll32 ordinal execution
// Status: Hunting query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint / DeviceProcessEvents
// Evidence: Cisco Talos observed 32-bit rundll32.exe executing disguised DLLs
// directly from WebDAV UNC paths through export ordinal #1.
// A match does not establish ClickFix delivery, Amatera execution, credential
// theft, NetSupport installation, C2, or compromise.
DeviceProcessEvents
| where FileName =~ "rundll32.exe"
| where ProcessCommandLine contains @"\\"
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "#1"
| project Timestamp, DeviceId, DeviceName, ActionType,
          FileName, FolderPath, ProcessCommandLine,
          SHA1, AccountDomain, AccountName, AccountUpn,
          InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessFolderPath,
          InitiatingProcessCommandLine, InitiatingProcessSHA1,
          ProcessIntegrityLevel, ProcessTokenElevation, ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
